00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:05,720
Here's a timeline we built of China,
from the first farming villages to the

2
00:00:05,770 --> 00:00:09,560
founding of the People's Republic in 1949.

3
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:13,110
Dynasties, reigns and
wars are bands; people,

4
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:19,090
books, inventions and battles are moments,
each with the source it draws on.

5
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:22,600
And almost everything with a name is
crowded into the last two and a half

6
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:24,229
thousand years.

7
00:00:25,779 --> 00:00:31,269
Zoom into the second millennium BCE.
Tradition says the first dynasty was the

8
00:00:31,319 --> 00:00:37,049
Xia; no writing of its own has
been found, so it's drawn dashed.

9
00:00:37,099 --> 00:00:40,449
The Shang are the first we can
read, in their oracle bones,

10
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:45,819
questions carved on bone and shell. The
early dates are the conventional ones,

11
00:00:45,869 --> 00:00:55,649
and approximate. The first year Chinese
history can date year by year is 841

12
00:00:55,699 --> 00:00:53,959
BCE.

13
00:01:00,869 --> 00:01:05,489
The Zhou last about eight centuries, while
its states grow into kingdoms and go

14
00:01:05,539 --> 00:01:11,689
to war. Then, in 221 BCE, Qin
conquers the last of them,

15
00:01:11,739 --> 00:01:16,569
and its king becomes Qin Shi
Huang, the First Emperor.

16
00:01:16,619 --> 00:01:21,823
His dynasty lasts fifteen years. The
Han that follows lasts four hundred.

17
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:27,603
Pull one thread out of the
rest. Separate by tags,

18
00:01:27,653 --> 00:01:31,263
choose thought, and the ideas
get a track of their own:

19
00:01:31,313 --> 00:01:36,053
Confucius, Laozi and Sunzi in
the same troubled centuries,

20
00:01:36,103 --> 00:01:40,643
the books burned under Qin, Confucian
learning made the state's under the Han,

21
00:01:40,693 --> 00:01:45,056
and examinations for office
that last until 1905.

22
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:52,036
Open a moment to read it. Sima Qian's
Records of the Grand Historian:

23
00:01:52,086 --> 00:01:55,086
what it is, how sure the date
is, where it comes from,

24
00:01:55,136 --> 00:02:01,005
and what it's linked to. His
tables are where 841 comes from.

25
00:02:02,725 --> 00:02:06,505
After the Han, China splits apart
for most of four centuries:

26
00:02:06,555 --> 00:02:11,055
the Three Kingdoms, the Jin,
dynasties north and south.

27
00:02:11,105 --> 00:02:16,115
Then it happens again. The
Sui reunite it in 589,

28
00:02:16,165 --> 00:02:20,805
dig the Grand Canal, and are
gone within thirty years.

29
00:02:20,855 --> 00:02:23,935
The Tang that follows lasts
nearly three centuries,

30
00:02:23,985 --> 00:02:27,275
and has the only woman to rule
as emperor in her own name,

31
00:02:27,325 --> 00:02:28,883
Wu Zetian.

32
00:02:30,613 --> 00:02:35,213
Choose invention instead:
irrigation, paper, a seismoscope,

33
00:02:35,263 --> 00:02:37,633
then the Song's paper money, movable type,

34
00:02:37,683 --> 00:02:41,353
gunpowder written down,
and the compass needle.

35
00:02:41,403 --> 00:02:44,603
And here is the oldest printed
book that carries its date,

36
00:02:44,653 --> 00:02:52,573
the Diamond Sutra. Its sources give
11 May 868 in the Julian calendar.

37
00:02:52,623 --> 00:02:55,913
The line is Gregorian throughout,
so it sits on the 15th,

38
00:02:55,963 --> 00:02:58,286
and the reader keeps both.

39
00:03:00,016 --> 00:03:04,736
Kublai Khan's Yuan rules
all of China from 1279.

40
00:03:04,786 --> 00:03:09,276
The Ming drive the Mongols out, and the
Yongle Emperor sends Zheng He's fleets

41
00:03:09,326 --> 00:03:13,496
as far as East Africa and
moves the capital to Beijing,

42
00:03:13,546 --> 00:03:18,366
to the Forbidden City. After a
Ming emperor is captured at Tumu,

43
00:03:18,416 --> 00:03:22,798
the dynasty builds the Great Wall
we know, in brick and stone.

44
00:03:24,518 --> 00:03:30,018
Then a century of wars: two Opium Wars,
the Taiping Rebellion between them,

45
00:03:30,068 --> 00:03:35,708
one of the deadliest wars in history,
and Cixi holding power for nearly fifty

46
00:03:35,758 --> 00:03:42,148
years. In 1912 the last emperor
abdicates. The Republic's civil war,

47
00:03:42,198 --> 00:03:47,418
paused but never settled, runs on either
side of eight years of war with Japan,

48
00:03:47,468 --> 00:03:53,748
and on 1 October 1949 Mao Zedong
proclaims the People's Republic.

49
00:03:53,798 --> 00:03:58,108
The link from the Treaty of Nanking
runs on to Hong Kong's return,

50
00:03:58,158 --> 00:04:00,132
in 1997.

51
00:04:01,682 --> 00:04:06,532
Anyone can read a public timeline
like this, no account needed.

52
00:04:06,582 --> 00:04:10,784
Check every date against its source,
or build your own with your class.
